      "widgets_values": [
        "MPI-361 PHASE A PROBE v2 - click-point masking, zero downloads\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Load Image -> pick a photo.\n2. Right-click it -> Open in MaskEditor.\n3. Dab SMALL DOTS on what you want. One dot per part.\n   Do NOT paint the object - just dab its centre. Brush ~16px.\n4. Save to node, Run.\n\nMultiple dots = multiple parts in ONE run (shirt + hair together).\nWant shirt then pants separately? Two runs. That is fine and expected.\n\nTHIS RUN IS NOW: RAW vs CLEANED, same mask.\nBroad/0.50 branch removed - tight is enough (your call).\n\n--- threshold ---\nSame knob as the old ComfyUI Preview Bridge 'confidence'. Confirmed.\nWHY NUDGING IT DOES NOTHING: SAM returns 3 candidate masks with\nscores. This keeps every candidate scoring >= threshold and unions\nthem; if none pass it falls back to the single best. So it only\nchanges when a candidate's SCORE falls between the old and new value.\n0.50 -> 0.60 = usually identical. SWEEP it (0.50 / 0.70 / 0.93 / 0.97),\ndo not nudge it. It steps, it does not ramp.\n\n--- dilation: LEAVE AT 0 ---\nConfirmed your read. It grows into unwanted areas because it is a\nblind dilate of whatever SAM returned, scatter included. The eraser\nbrush is the better answer.\n\n--- THE SCATTER FIX (the real problem) ---\nLoose specks and pinholes cost real time downstream: the detailer\nmasks each zone INDIVIDUALLY, so a stray speck becomes a wasted\ndetail pass. Same complaint you have with detect-person.\n\nCleanup = morphological OPEN then CLOSE, 2 nodes, no new weights:\n  erode -4   -> detached specks thinner than 8px vanish\n  dilate +4  -> genuine mask returns to its true size\n  fill_holes -> pinholes inside the mask close\n\nCompare the two previews. Tune the pair TOGETHER - they must stay\nequal and opposite or the mask grows or shrinks overall.\n  4/4  gentle - kills dust only\n  6/6  moderate - what most people want\n  10/10 aggressive - also eats fingers, straps, thin hair strands\n\nIf cleanup eats something you needed, that is the ceiling of this\napproach - lower the pair, do not raise dilation.\n\nZERO DOWNLOADS - sam_vit_b_01ec64.pth already ships with the app.\n\n--- YOUR NOTES BELOW ---\n"
      ]
    },
